# Line-ending and binary handling.
#
# Contributors run with core.autocrlf=true on Windows, so without these rules
# git decides per file, by heuristic, whether to rewrite line endings on
# checkout. That guess is right almost always, and silently destructive when it
# is not: a font rewritten as text stops parsing, and the browser falls back to
# a substitute face with no error anywhere. Declare the binary formats instead
# of relying on the guess.

* text=auto

# Fonts. These ship with the vendored KaTeX and must survive a checkout intact,
# including on an air-gapped host where nothing can be re-downloaded.
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.otf   binary

# Images and other binary assets.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.bmp   binary
*.tif   binary
*.tiff  binary
*.ico   binary

# Model checkpoints and archives.
*.pt    binary
*.pth   binary
*.ckpt  binary
*.onnx  binary
*.h5    binary
*.hdf5  binary
*.pkl   binary
*.npy   binary
*.npz   binary
*.zip   binary

# Office documents.
*.docx  binary
*.pptx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.pdf   binary

# SVG is text and benefits from normal diffing.
*.svg   text
